WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:04.384
"There's one!"

2
00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:07.865
Raj tried to catch a hopping cricket.

3
00:00:07.965 --> 00:00:14.407
"Oops! I missed it!"

4
00:00:14.427 --> 00:00:32.884
"That's because you used your hands," Parker said.

5
00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:34.565
"I'll get them with my feet!"

6
00:00:35.386 --> 00:00:37.587
He lifted a foot to stomp on a cricket.

7
00:00:37.947 --> 00:00:39.188
Daisy grabbed his arm.

8
00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:43.130
"No!" "Hey, you made me miss it!"

9
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.331
Parker cried.

10
00:00:44.351 --> 00:00:48.393
"Daisy would never let you hurt an animal," Kaleem said.

11
00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:52.535
"Right," Raj said, staring at Daisy.

12
00:00:52.555 --> 00:00:59.739
"She wanted us to let the crickets out of the tank, and now—" "They're out of the tank!"

13
00:01:00.279 --> 00:01:00.960
Parker said.

14
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.621
He narrowed his eyes.

15
00:01:02.641 --> 00:01:05.082
"Did you let them out, Birdbrain?"

16
00:01:06.442 --> 00:01:08.683
Mr. Neal hurried into the classroom.

17
00:01:08.703 --> 00:01:11.124
"I just heard a cricket chirping in the hall."

18
00:01:12.545 --> 00:01:16.306
He gasped when he saw the overturned tank.

19
00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:17.267
"Oh no!"

20
00:01:17.287 --> 00:01:20.868
"Daisy let the crickets go," Parker said.

21
00:01:20.888 --> 00:01:23.109
"I did not!"

22
00:01:23.389 --> 00:01:24.190
Daisy cried.

23
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:29.812
"Daisy didn't do it," Grace said shyly.

24
00:01:30.948 --> 00:01:34.371
"She was with me for the entire recess period."

25
00:01:35.312 --> 00:01:36.993
"We can figure out what happened later."

26
00:01:38.074 --> 00:01:40.917
Mr. Neal made shooing motions with his hands.

27
00:01:40.937 --> 00:01:44.180
"Everyone, back outside, please.

28
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.563
I'll ask the janitor to sweep the crickets out of the building."

29
00:01:49.164 --> 00:01:50.125
"Sweep them?"

30
00:01:50.565 --> 00:01:51.926
Daisy was horrified.

31
00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.451
Mr. Neal sighed.

32
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.162
"I'll ask him to try not to hurt them.

33
00:02:02.463 --> 00:02:03.723
Now go outside, everyone!"

34
00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:11.089
Daisy walked out to the playground with Kaleem and Grace.

35
00:02:15.132 --> 00:02:18.995
if the janitor is careful with the broom, some crickets might be hurt."

36
00:02:20.376 --> 00:02:21.516
Raj overheard her.

37
00:02:21.536 --> 00:02:24.579
"So what, Daisy?

38
00:02:24.899 --> 00:02:26.000
They're just bugs."

39
00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:30.006
Daisy shook her head, and looked around for Beatrice.

40
00:02:30.987 --> 00:02:34.409
Most people would say that the bumblebee was just a bug too.

41
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.771
But she was Daisy's friend.

42
00:02:38.012 --> 00:02:42.295
Daisy didn't see Beatrice, but she did see a cricket hopping out the door.

43
00:02:47.198 --> 00:02:48.099
be right back."

44
00:02:48.759 --> 00:02:50.200
She hurried over to the cricket.

45
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.023
"I'm finally free!"

46
00:02:54.583 --> 00:02:55.164
he chirped.

47
00:02:56.736 --> 00:02:58.877
Daisy kneeled down to whisper to him.

48
00:02:58.897 --> 00:03:00.997
"I'm glad you're free.

49
00:03:02.458 --> 00:03:04.858
But we need to warn your friends about something."

50
00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:08.419
She told the cricket about the janitor with the broom.

51
00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:11.960
"Oh, dear," the cricket said.

52
00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.741
"I'll see what I can do."

53
00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:16.642
Daisy looked up.

54
00:03:17.842 --> 00:03:20.003
Mr. Neal was still inside the building.

55
00:03:20.923 --> 00:03:21.383
So Mrs.

56
00:03:21.463 --> 00:03:24.164
Petty, the art teacher, was watching their class.

57
00:03:24.956 --> 00:03:27.661
Luckily, she wasn't looking in Daisy's direction.

58
00:03:28.802 --> 00:03:31.346
Daisy usually obeyed the rules at school.

59
00:03:32.027 --> 00:03:33.690
But this was an emergency.

60
00:03:36.955 --> 00:03:39.860
Moving fast, she sneaked back into the building.

61
00:03:54.376 --> 00:03:57.737
She hurried up and down the hall, looking and listening for crickets.

62
00:03:59.297 --> 00:04:03.018
Every time she found one, she offered to carry it outside.

63
00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:08.380
Soon her pockets were full of crickets.

64
00:04:12.781 --> 00:04:13.741
Finally Mr.

65
00:04:13.821 --> 00:04:14.722
Neal spotted her.

66
00:04:14.742 --> 00:04:17.022
"What are you doing inside, Daisy?"

67
00:04:17.042 --> 00:04:18.743
"I'm sorry."

68
00:04:19.423 --> 00:04:22.764
Daisy hoped the crickets in her pockets wouldn't chirp and give her away.

69
00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:27.445
"I came in to, um, use the bathroom."

70
00:04:29.105 --> 00:04:31.186
She scurried outside before Mr.

71
00:04:31.306 --> 00:04:32.406
Neal could respond.

72
00:04:33.847 --> 00:04:35.127
Kaleem was waiting for her.

73
00:04:35.147 --> 00:04:36.728
"Did you get all the crickets?"

74
00:04:38.148 --> 00:04:38.968
"I hope so."

75
00:04:40.149 --> 00:04:42.349
Daisy helped the crickets out of her pockets.

76
00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.411
They hopped away into the bushes, chirping happily.

77
00:04:47.431 --> 00:04:49.712
"We're free!

78
00:04:49.872 --> 00:04:50.712
We're free!"

79
00:04:52.044 --> 00:04:53.125
"Thank you, Daisy!"

80
00:04:53.505 --> 00:04:54.647
a few crickets said.

81
00:04:55.647 --> 00:04:56.708
Daisy smiled.

82
00:04:56.728 --> 00:04:58.350
"You're welcome."

83
00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:02.434
"Uh-oh." Kaleem was staring past her.

84
00:05:02.454 --> 00:05:04.516
"Here comes the janitor!"
